Zodiak - Earth terrain analogs for the lunar south pole
NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026, team Zodiak (Poznań)

The original code of this repository is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE).
It was written by the team with Super Intelligence (SI) assistance (Claude Code, Antigravity, OpenAI Codex);
the team chose the problem, the research goals and the interpretation (README.md, "Team, SI and licence").

This repository bundles or redistributes the following third-party material. Each keeps its own terms.

1. Leaflet 1.9.4 (app/vendor/leaflet.js, app/vendor/leaflet.css)
   https://leafletjs.com/ - BSD 2-Clause License, full text in app/vendor/LICENSE-Leaflet.
   app/app.js loads the same version from https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/ when the bundled copy fails its
   integrity check.

2. Natural Earth (app/assets/land.geojson: ne_110m_land; country lookups in pipeline/sites.py from
   https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector, v5.1.2)
   https://www.naturalearthdata.com/ - public domain ("Made with Natural Earth").

3. NASA imagery and data products (data/sites/images/, data/validation/landcover_sensitivity/images/,
   app/data/img/, data/moon/): NASA Worldview / GIBS true-colour imagery (MODIS, VIIRS, HLS), LRO LOLA, Diviner,
   Mini-RF, LAMP, LEND and LROC products. NASA open data; credits per file in data/sources.csv and README.md.
   GIBS acknowledgement: "We acknowledge the use of imagery provided by services from NASA's Global Imagery
   Browse Services (GIBS), part of NASA's Earth Science Data and Information System (ESDIS)."

4. Derived data from ESA WorldCover 2021 v200 (CC BY 4.0; (c) ESA WorldCover project 2021 / Contains modified
   Copernicus Sentinel data (2021) processed by ESA WorldCover consortium; Zanaga et al. 2022,
   doi:10.5281/zenodo.7254221) and Copernicus DEM GLO-30 ("produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 (c) DLR e.V.
   2010-2014 and (c) Airbus Defence and Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and
   ESA; all rights reserved"), in data/earth/ and data/sites/.

5. Place names from OpenStreetMap (Nominatim, Overpass): (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL 1.0.

6. Adapted globe and terrain code in web/src/ (MIT), with the license and copyright notice
   in web/public/licenses/atlas-mit.txt. Globe imagery products are credited in web/public/textures/README.md.

Every external dataset, service and library with its licence or citation: data/sources.csv (generated by
pipeline/catalog.py) and README.md, section "Data and acknowledgements".

No image in this repository was generated by an SI image model: figures and maps are rendered from data with
matplotlib or are screenshots of the web app; satellite and lunar images are the providers' products. No NASA
logo or insignia is used.
